// A comparison handed an array answers one for each of what it holds,
// so this function's body hands back bool[] where its signature says
// bool.  The parameter's declared type is what settles it, so it is
// settled before anything runs and reported whether or not the
// function is ever called — nothing here calls it.
fn g3(x : i32[]) → bool:
    x > 3

@start
fn main():
    std.println("not reached")
